What this library does not ship
-------------------------------

* No scrapers. The library contains no scrapers and does not fetch or
  parse third-party web pages; it only normalises text found in feeds and API
  responses it is given (HTML tags in feed content are stripped). It has no
  headless browsers or scraping proxies. Hosts that need a scraper implement
  the out.Scraper port themselves.
* No data. It contains no real articles, sources, dictionaries, entity
  catalogs, rosters, trained models or datasets. Every fixture and example
  file is synthetic: fictional teams and people, example.com hosts.
* No credentials. API keys, bot tokens and session files are supplied by the
  host program at run time and never stored in this repository.

Whoever runs the engine chooses its sources and is responsible for having
the right to fetch, process and republish their content.

Third-party data and services
-----------------------------

* nflverse roster data. The roster sync (packages infra/nflverse and
  infra/nflverse/rostersync, command "entities roster sync") downloads roster
  files published by the nflverse project
  (https://github.com/nflverse/nflverse-data). That data is licensed under
  the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Credit the nflverse project
  when you redistribute data derived from it. No roster data is included in
  this repository.
* ESPN scoreboard. The match-state adapter (adapters/outbound/espnscoreboard)
  reads a public scoreboard JSON endpoint that is undocumented and
  unofficial. It may change, be rate limited or be restricted at any time
  without notice. It is disabled by default; enabling it is at your own risk,
  and you must respect the provider's terms of use.
* Reddit, Bluesky, YouTube, Telegram, Wikidata, SearXNG and Tavily are
  reached through their public or official APIs and are subject to their own
  terms of service and rate limits. Wikidata content is CC0.

